  "index": 33,
  "text": "The optimal doses of antiangiogenic agents contribute to improving TIME 27. A previous study shows that anlotinib (3 mg/kg) boosts radioimmunotherapy efficacy 28. However, it did not examine dose effects on TIME. In the current study, anlotinib (3 mg/kg) plus radiation did not increase CD8+ T cells versus IR alone (Supplementary Fig. 8). Anlotinib (1.5 mg/kg) reportedly breaks through the immunosuppressive barrier to potentiate TIME 29. Consistently, low-dose (1.5 mg/kg) anlotinib plus IR normalized vessels (Supplementary Fig. 9) and was therefore selected for subsequent experiments. However, the optimal dose remains controversial and requires further study.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
